{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0214", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Sch_\\etale$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$S_{affine, \\etale} \\to S_\\etale$", "MATH_0005": "$\\Sh(S_{affine, \\etale})$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Sh(S_\\etale)$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-alternative}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:63323a6d47b6642a88423a54338a8211b202b6e25b7e65598dd122522bb707a5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9ee32f01059ee15321cbd0f3ac21eb0e12c6e31ee18ebcbc4ae3853412060c91", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a big <ACCENT_0001>tale\nsite containing <MATH_0003>. The functor <MATH_0004>\nis special cocontinuous and induces an equivalence of topoi from\n<MATH_0005> to <MATH_0006>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2270a476e92bda95eb591de48938259fc29924179f2c22cb3abc6f53e914af43", "unit_id": "tag:04HR:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0214", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-affine-big-site-etale}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:43f6656219b60ee0569f4257744c4ef4b096c525b7b246ad9d8959c342a2370f", "source_text": "Omitted. Hint: compare with the proof of\nLemma <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:912538f05aa3ff64c4821db2b28a8ed657f8a86d24f72dfcb3b308a7aedc2ebc", "unit_id": "tag:04HR:proof"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0214", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8295c69207808d7b45acba3e72a5825152106b5efb306553878b66565613be80", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nNext, we establish some relationships between the topoi\nassociated to these sites.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c1180215722ae63882047268b44a72225f372a791bf36a874a5e1330a20dd47d", "unit_id": "tag:0214:prose-0008"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0214", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$\\Sch_\\etale$", "MATH_0002": "$f : T \\to S$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Sch_\\etale$", "MATH_0004": "$T_\\etale \\to (\\Sch/S)_\\etale$", "MATH_0005": "$$\ni_f :\n\\Sh(T_\\etale)\n\\longrightarrow\n\\Sh((\\Sch/S)_\\etale)\n$$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0007": "$(\\Sch/S)_\\etale$", "MATH_0008": "$(i_f^{-1}\\mathcal{G})(U/T) = \\mathcal{G}(U/S)$", "MATH_0009": "$i_f^{-1}$", "MATH_0010": "$i_{f, !}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-put-in-T-etale}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a210a763b29e9d88729da249ab0c91db575218285f023e4d46554427502b865e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c18dca5e2ffd00e22485cab3daa11c1a08a071101b5ce63408a36b9746cfe759", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a big <ACCENT_0001>tale site.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a morphism in <MATH_0003>.\nThe functor <MATH_0004>\nis cocontinuous and induces a morphism of topoi\n<MATH_0005>\nFor a sheaf <MATH_0006> on <MATH_0007>\nwe have the formula <MATH_0008>.\nThe functor <MATH_0009> also has a left adjoint <MATH_0010> which commutes\nwith fibre products and equalizers.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4865592046e78ea81ea9375c94c5f4f3b7c6eadc5ee6adb5a4a8ebe0f9f2ed09", "unit_id": "tag:021F:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0214", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0003": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$u : T_\\etale \\to (\\Sch/S)_\\etale$", "MATH_0002": "$j : U \\to T$", "MATH_0003": "$T_\\etale$", "MATH_0004": "$u(U \\to T) = (f \\circ j : U \\to S)$", "MATH_0005": "$a, b : U \\to V$", "MATH_0006": "$T_\\etale$", "MATH_0007": "$a$", "MATH_0008": "$b$", "MATH_0009": "$$\nV \\times_{\\Delta_{V/T}, V \\times_T V, (a, b)} U\n$$", "MATH_0010": "$T$", "MATH_0011": "$T$", "MATH_0012": "$T_\\etale$", "MATH_0013": "$u$", "MATH_0014": "$u$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-fibre-products-etale}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{sites-lemma-when-shriek}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{sites-lemma-preserve-equalizers}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:665184e7bbeda8658da89a5d887d0c93903f3fc4882a0fa70b043ee01f620d5f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:42c219877d5321412150f75e1472d6f0dc1b80d995e091db392cefdfaf00ffe1", "source_text": "Denote the functor <MATH_0001>.\nIn other words, given an <ACCENT_0001>tale morphism <MATH_0002> corresponding\nto an object of <MATH_0003> we set <MATH_0004>.\nThis functor commutes with fibre products, see\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nLet <MATH_0005> be two morphisms in <MATH_0006>.\nIn this case the equalizer of <MATH_0007> and <MATH_0008> (in the category of schemes) is\n<MATH_0009>\nwhich is a fibre product of schemes <ACCENT_0002>tale over <MATH_0010>, hence <ACCENT_0003>tale\nover <MATH_0011>. Thus <MATH_0012> has equalizers and <MATH_0013> commutes with them.\nIt is clearly cocontinuous.\nIt is also continuous as <MATH_0014> transforms coverings to coverings and\ncommutes with fibre products. Hence the Lemma follows from\nSites, Lemmas <REF_0002>\nand <REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ecc379c2a1eba1788d49892f95e36244df0dcaae6689d3c4acc5edceb2df39e5", "unit_id": "tag:021F:proof"}
